{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And YHWH Elohim caused to fall</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the others: \"and it fell upon him and he died,\" \"and it fell in the midst of his camp.\" This is what they said of one who killed unintentionally and one who killed intentionally, that HaShem arranges them in one inn, and one goes up a ladder, etc. And this is \"and it fell in the midst of his camp\" — that HaShem arranges them in his camp." "<b>and He closed</b> Two times in the Masorah: here, and: \"and YHWH closed [the ark] for him.\" A hint to the closing of flesh — that they were forbidden in marital relations in the ark, when YHWH closed [it] for him — then: \"and flesh was closed.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The three Masorah occurrences cited are: ויפל ה' אלהים (here, Genesis 2:21), ויפל עליו וימות (Joshua 20:9 region), and ויפל בקרב מחנהו (possibly Judges 7:13 or cognate; left unaddressed as per protocol).", 1 "The second occurrence cited is ויסגור ה' בעדו (Genesis 7:16). The phrase 'ויסגור בשר' is rendered hyper-literally as 'and flesh was closed'; possibly a wordplay on בשר תחת בשר whose exact sense is left as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:35.961479069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}